cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference BeigeWall, please cite it as below."
title: "BeigeWall: an adversarial-agent authority and evidence-custody research vertical"
abstract: >-
  BeigeWall is a research artifact investigating whether an untrusted agent can
  stay useful when the authority, disclosure, effect, resource, and evidence
  boundaries do not depend on trusting it. It progresses from in-process
  mediation through a process boundary, resource bounds, durable and independent
  evidence custody, a VM/KVM boundary, and recoverable evidence. Synthetic
  corpus; standard-library Python; not a production system.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The BeigeWall Authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/unpingable/beigewall"
url: "https://github.com/unpingable/beigewall"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
keywords:
  - adversarial agents
  - capability security
  - authority mediation
  - evidence custody
  - provenance
  - LLM agents
